    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d281">

                <pb facs="0392" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg272"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Squiers to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Habana,
                                Cuba</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-05-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1241.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * With reference to contract for
                    sewering and paying Habana, I have the honor to inclose translation of a
                    Presidential message sent to Congress April 28 and a newspaper report<anchor
                        n="a" xml:id="d281-f1"/> of the debate following the reading of the message
                    in the Senate.</p>
                <p>Mr. O’Farrill in a recent interview agreed that a message should be prepared and
                    sent to Congress.</p>
                <p>Mr. Palma’s prompt action indicates the pressure of interested persons who will
                    without doubt push matters to a favorable issue, if it is possible to do so. * *
                    *</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. G. Squiers.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d281-a1.xml" xpointer="d281-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
